  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Randomised evaluation of a preventive intervention for postnatal depression in high-risk populations in Pakistan and Turkey: PREVENT-PND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MRC AGHRB Award to evaluate a psychosocial group intervention to prevent postnatal depression (PND), a disorder of public health significance, in women who live in socioeconomically deprived communities and are at high risk for the condition in Turkey and Pakistan</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The overarching aim of our project is to evaluate a psychosocial group intervention to prevent postnatal depression (PND), a disorder of public health significance, in women who live in socioeconomically deprived communities and are at high risk for the condition. 
In the last decade we have worked with our Pakistani partners to develop and evaluate psychosocial treatments for perinatal depression. In a recently concluded MRC-funded seed grant, we worked with our Pakistani and Turkish partners to develop a cognitive behaviour therapy-based group intervention to prevent perinatal depression. We successfully conducted a feasibility study of this intervention in poor localities in Istanbul. In the current project, we aim to conduct a definitive Randomised Controlled Trial (RCT) in two countries, Turkey and Pakistan, to address the following objectives: 
a) Evaluate the effectiveness, and cost-effectiveness, of the group intervention in preventing postnatal depression in high-risk women in two diverse settings. 
b) Determine if the intervention improves functioning, maternal attachment, and childcare abilities.
c) Explore the mechanisms through which the intervention achieves its effects.  
d) Build capacity in the two countries for implementation research that can assist with the future scale-up of such interventions. &quot;</narrative>
  </description>
